\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qc\highlight1\kerning2\b\f0\fs28\lang16393 Day 11 Capstone \endash  ShopKart Order API\highlight0\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\fs24\par
1. Project Overview\par
\b0 ShopKart is an online shopping application for which I developed a backend REST API using Python, Flask and Pydantic.\par
The main purpose of this project is to handle product listing, cart bill calculations, discount coupons, customer details validation and order placement.\par
The backend allows customers to view products, calculate their total bill, apply discounts, place orders and retrieve their order details.\par
\par
\b 2. Technologies Used\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1 Python:\b0  Used to develop the backend application and implement business logic.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b Flask:\b0  Used to create REST APIs and handle HTTP requests.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b Pydantic:\b0  Used to validate customer details, product IDs, quantities and other input data.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b YAML:\b0  Used to store business configurations such as GST percentage, shipping charges and coupon rules.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b JSON:\b0  Used to store product information, including product ID, name, category, price and stock.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b Pytest:\b0  Used to write and execute automated test cases.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b VS Code REST Client:\b0  Used to send API requests and test different functionalities directly from VS Code.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b Python Logging:\b0  Used to record application activities, information and errors.\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\par
\b 3. Project Implementation\par
3.1 Project Structure\par
\b0 Created a layered project structure to organise the application properly. Each file is responsible for a specific task.\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\b Config:\b0  Stores application settings and business rules.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b Schemas:\b0  Defines data models and validates incoming requests using Pydantic.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b Services:\b0  Handles business logic such as pricing, coupon calculations and order processing.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b Repository:\b0  Handles reading and updating product information from the JSON file.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b Routes:\b0  Defines API endpoints and handles incoming requests.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b Exceptions:\b0  Contains custom exception classes for handling application errors.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b Logging Setup:\b0  Configures application logs for monitoring activities and errors.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b Tests:\b0  Contains automated test cases for checking application functionality.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b run.py:\b0  Used to start the Flask application on port 8000.\par

