\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\i Figure 1: ShopKart Flask application started successfully on port 8000. The terminal shows product loading, API requests, order creation and stock validation logs.\i0\par
\b 3.2 Configuration Management\par
\b0 Configured the application using YAML files to maintain business values separately from the Python code.\par
Configured GST at 18%, shipping charges of \f2\u8377?\f0 49, free shipping above \f2\u8377?\f0 999 and coupon rules for FEST20 and WELCOME10.\par
Also configured the application environment as development and implemented logging to display application activities in the console and log file.\par
\b 3.3 Product Management API\par
\b0 Created an API to retrieve all available products from the JSON file.\par
Implemented category-based filtering so customers can view products belonging to a particular category, such as electronics.\par
\b 3.4 Cart Quote and Pricing Calculation\par
\b0 Implemented the Cart Quote API to calculate the customer's bill before placing an order.\par
The calculation includes:\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1 Product subtotal.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Discount based on the applied coupon.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}GST calculation after discount.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Shipping charges based on cart value.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Final payable amount.\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1 Implemented FEST20 (20% discount) and WELCOME10 (10% discount) with minimum cart value conditions.\par
The Cart Quote API calculates the bill without changing the product stock.\par
\b 3.5 Order Management\par
\b0 Implemented the Order API to accept customer details, selected products and delivery address.\par
Before placing an order, the application checks whether the requested product quantities are available in stock.\par
After successful validation and stock checking, an order is created with a unique order ID, such as SK-1001.\par
The application also supports retrieving an existing order using its order ID.\par
\b 3.6 Input Validation and Error Handling\par
\b0 Used Pydantic to validate customer information and incoming API requests.\par
Implemented validation for email, six-digit pincode, Indian mobile number and product quantity.\par
Created custom exceptions to handle errors such as invalid products, invalid requests and insufficient stock.\par
The application returns appropriate HTTP status codes such as 404, 409 and 422 for different errors.\par
\b 3.7 Logging and Monitoring\par
\b0 Implemented logging to monitor application activities and errors.\par
The application displays log messages in the terminal and also writes logs to a log file.\par
Used INFO and DEBUG logging levels depending on the application environment.\par
\b\par
4. API Testing Using VS Code REST Client\par
\b0 Integrated the REST Client extension in VS Code with the api_requests.http file to simplify API testing.\par
Created and organised different HTTP requests in a single file to test the available API endpoints.\par
The file contains GET and POST requests for:\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1 Health check.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Product listing with category filtering.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Cart quote and coupon calculation.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Order creation.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Retrieving order details.\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1 Used the \b Send Request\b0  option provided by the REST Client extension to execute requests directly from the .http file.\par
The API responses, including HTTP status codes and JSON output, were displayed directly inside VS Code.\par
This made API testing easier because requests could be executed with a single click without repeatedly entering commands in the terminal or using external API testing tools and also tested different scenarios by modifying request data, such as entering an invalid pincode and requesting products with unavailable stock, to verify input validation and error handling.\par
